& [QueryModuleSet] is the executable boundary
  + [fabric] is an immutable in-memory projection of admitted packages using the admission-verified signed exact label index plus package-owner and relation indexes
  + [engine] is request validation, exact identity and alias resolution, deterministic lexical candidate fallback, contextual filtering, typed traversal, projection, detail accounting, proof assembly, visible faults, and result digest verification
  + [metrics] is package, unit, relation, signed-source-byte, and serialized-package-byte accounting

& [ResolutionDecisionSet] is the implemented meaning
  + [order] is trust snapshot before exact identity or opt-in lexical fallback candidates, context, typed relationships, projection, and proof
  + [context] is subject, purpose, use case, source scope, perspective, include boundary, exclude boundary, criteria, and description need
  + [ambiguity] is equally applicable meanings remain present and faulted rather than collapsed
  + [known_units] is exact resident units may resolve without record retransmission and receive an AlreadyResident account while new source, path, or authority detail remains eligible
  + [relationship] is each path contains package-bound typed relation steps rather than unexplained hop identities
  + [quote] is each returned quote carries its source anchor, whole-document digest, certificate identity, and verified status
  + [authority] is read-only semantic access checked against caller and recognized package scopes
  + [budgets] is records, paths, traversal depth, serialized record bytes, and elapsed time
  + [digest] is the normalized complete result and structured proof are SHA-256 bound and independently recomputable

& [FaultDecisionSet] is visible
  + [unknown] is an unmatched term without making the request structurally invalid
  + [invalid] is a rejected protocol, empty semantic demand, invalid budget, or invalid operation boundary
  + [unauthorized] is a recognized candidate outside caller read scope
  + [ambiguous] is a tied contextual meaning set
  + [contradictory] is an explicit Contradicts edge on a returned typed path
  + [budget_clipped] is deterministic record, byte, path, depth, or elapsed truncation
  + [missing_detail] is an explicit account when admitted material cannot supply a requested record kind
  + [stale] is rejected before fabric construction by Slice 02 admission and therefore cannot masquerade as an empty query result

& [DeliberateLimitationSet] is retained
  + [persistence] is in-memory only pending observed workload evidence
  + [lexical] is deterministic substring containment and is reported separately from exact identity
  + [routing] is Routed and Composed search remain visibly unsupported and grant no authority
  + [factual_truth] is proof establishes admitted-source lineage and engine selection, not universal exterior truth
  + [derivation] is returned only for already compiled inferred units; no new inference calculus is introduced here
  + [cross_package_relation] is absent because this baseline requires both relation endpoints inside one signed package; a link authority profile must precede cross-package edges
  - never: interpret score, path distance, lexical containment, or result digest as semantic authority

& [SolutionDisposition] is accepted
